taSeconds":719}}},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":7,"finishersRank":10,"finishRateRank":96,"winningTimeRank":40,"winningTimeRankDir":17,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1966,"mensWinner":"Tommy MALONE","mensTime":"06:14:07"}},"narrative":"The 2015 Comrades Marathon was the 90th running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 87.720 kms. The race was held on Sunday, 31 May. Conditions: Mild at start. Warming to hot late morning to mid afternoon. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nGift KELEHE claimed the men's title in 05:38:36, ahead of Mohammed HUSIEN (05:46:14) and Hatiwande NYAMANDE (05:48:19). Caroline CHERRY won the women's race in 06:12:22, followed by Charne BOSMAN (06:33:24).\n\nCaroline CHERRY's 06:12:22 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1966 (Tommy MALONE, 06:14:07).\n\nFrom a field of 22,418 entries, 12,735 runners crossed the finish line (56.8% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 10,237 men and 2,497 women (19.6% female). The average finish time was 10:28:07.\n\nMedals awarded: 19 Gold, 405 Silver, 1,671 Bill Rowan, 5,440 Bronze, 5,200 Vic Clapham. 3,116 runners (24.5%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Philip GRAY in 12:00:00.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 2011, the field was 14.7% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 56% of the finishers, with 5,614 seniors (avg 10:16:32) and 7,120 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}